  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "h4IR0vB682HiAHtYGUIx8qLN1Xg=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:29:22.034Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The spec opens with the failure that motivated it, and the failure is worth keeping on its own.\n\nMapping between GraphQL payloads and the domain `Operation` was manual and done in **several places**, so it drifted:\n\n- the **PullResponder query omitted `actionId`**, yet the domain `Operation.action.id` requires it \u2014 this compiled and produced `undefined` at runtime;\n- in the **DriveSubgraph resolver**, GraphQL op fields were spread into the domain `Operation`, which put `type` at the operation root and duplicated `scope` / `branch` at the wrong level instead of nesting them under `action`.\n\nWhy the tests did not catch it is the more transferable part:\n\n1. the GraphQL query and mutation **strings were not type-checked against the schema** \u2014 there was no codegen;\n2. there was **no runtime decoding or validation** at the boundaries;\n3. the unit tests **did not assert on the exact DTO\u2194domain mapping**, nor on required fields like `actionId`.\n\nAny hand-written GraphQL string in this codebase is exposed to all three, which is the argument for generated documents and a validating decode step rather than for more careful review.\n\n## Provenance\n- `docs/specs/gql-gen.md` \u2014 Concrete Break Example: Sync Path\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:29:22.034Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:29:22.034Z"
    }
  },
  {
    "index": 4,
    "hash": "",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:30:25.422Z",
    "action": {
